izes and potential shapes, especially comparing the shapes of all components in Train 1 and Train 4, looking for parallels.\n\n\n**Evaluating 2x2 Square Patterns**\n\nI'm now investigating a new hypothesis, and I see the total count of 2s in each training example, and how many transformed to 6.  I'm now focused on 2x2 squares, and checking for a 2x2 window with at least three 2s, in all the training data. For example, looking at a 2x2 square in Train 1.\n\n\n**Analyzing 2x2 Square Components**\n\nI've been reexamining the training data, focusing on size-3 components and their behavior in Train 3. I've confirmed that the size-3 component, despite having a 2x2 bounding box, remains unchanged. It did not transform to size 6. This suggests the width/height is not the sole factor.\n\n\n\n",
